1
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:09,950
In the spring of 1453, a city that had stood for eleven hundred years was about to fall.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,650
Its walls had turned back army after army.

3
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:17,750
Its emperor had perhaps seven thousand men to hold them.

4
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:25,950
Facing him: tens of thousands of soldiers, a twenty-one-year-old sultan, and a very large cannon.

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:31,450
Now, you would think a thousand years of history might buy you a little more time.

6
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:38,800
But history, as it turns out, has never once accepted a loyalty card.
